# TypeScript Standards

{{#if parameters.strictNullChecks}}
- Enable strict null checks; never use `any` to bypass nullability
- Use optional chaining and nullish coalescing over manual null checks
{{/if}}
{{#if parameters.preferInterfaces}}
- Prefer `interface` over `type` for object shapes
{{/if}}
- Keep functions under {{parameters.maxFunctionLines}} lines; extract helpers when larger
{{#if parameters.strictErrors}}
- Never swallow errors in empty catch blocks
- Wrap errors with context using `cause` when re-throwing
- Define typed error classes for domain failures
{{/if}}
- Use exhaustive switch with `never` check in default case for discriminated unions
